      "message": "In this CL, we introduced a speed feature `skip_loop_filter_using_filt_error` for low-complexity decode mode. This sf resets luma filter levels based on relative reduction in error when applying the filter compared to no filtering for the current frame. This sf is not enabled for pyramid_level \u003e 1 to contain the BD-rate drop.\n\nThe visual quality tests showed no artifacts for mid and high bit-rates for cpu \u003c\u003d 3.\n\nPerformance results of encoder and decoder for the streams generated\nwith low complexity decode enabled.\n\n```\n                       Instruction Count                                                                              \n                          Reduction(%)                   BD-Rate Loss(%)                Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr     ssim       vmaf    vmaf_neg    dav1d Decoder   \n   1          608P      -0.098     3.136      0.1330     0.2940    -0.0128     0.0158       3.120\n   1        HDRES2      -0.168     6.650      0.4240     0.5649     0.2104     0.2103       6.987\n   1       Average      -0.130     4.733      0.2653     0.4171     0.0887     0.1042       4.878\n   \n   2          608P      -0.095     3.294      0.1534     0.3535     0.0287     0.0328       3.383\n   2        HDRES2      -0.106     6.815      0.4890     0.5839     0.2491     0.2381       6.748\n   2       Average      -0.100     4.894      0.3059     0.4582     0.1289     0.1261       4.913\n   \n   3          608P      -0.043     3.551      0.1778     0.3155    -0.0268    -0.0272       3.240\n   3        HDRES2       0.001     7.031      0.4333     0.4881     0.1044     0.1033       7.123\n   3       Average      -0.023     5.133      0.2939     0.3940     0.0328     0.0321       5.005  \n   \n```\n\nThe instruction count reduction specified has been measured using command:\n`$ perf stat -e instructions:u ./aomenc …`\n`$ perf stat -e instructions:u ./dav1d --cpumask avx2 …`\n\nThe 